      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "When the Fed moves interest rates, how fast does your credit card follow?",
        "start": 0.27,
        "seconds": 3.28,
        "window": 3.87,
        "fill": 0.848
      },
      {
        "scene": "headline",
        "text": "In September, the Fed raised its target range by a quarter point, to 4% at the top.",
        "start": 4.13,
        "seconds": 4.59,
        "window": 5.2,
        "fill": 0.883
      },
      {
        "scene": "chain",
        "text": "Banks move their prime rate with it. And most card rates are prime plus a margin.",
        "start": 9.33,
        "seconds": 3.78,
        "window": 4.37,
        "fill": 0.865
      },
      {
        "scene": "fast",
        "text": "So within a billing cycle or two, your rate moves too.",
        "start": 13.7,
        "seconds": 2.53,
        "window": 3.13,
        "fill": 0.808
      },
      {
        "scene": "rates",
        "text": "Say you carry $6,000 at 22%. A quarter point more makes it 22.25%.",
        "start": 16.83,
        "seconds": 5.72,
        "window": 6.3,
        "fill": 0.908
      },
      {
        "scene": "interest",
        "text": "Paying only the minimum, the total interest goes from $7,948 to $8,172.",
        "start": 23.13,
        "seconds": 6.95,
        "window": 7.57,
        "fill": 0.918
      },
      {
        "scene": "stack",
        "text": "Small on its own. But every move stacks on the last one.",
        "start": 30.7,
        "seconds": 2.74,
        "window": 3.37,
        "fill": 0.813
      },
      {
        "scene": "outro",
        "text": "So, do you know your card's rate?",
